Comment: The pex bundles second-hand's runtime dependencies at the versions
 pinned in uv.lock. Each keeps its own license and copyright notice inside the
 pex, in its .dist-info directory; list them with:
 .
   unzip -l /usr/lib/second-hand/second-hand.pex '.deps/*.dist-info/*'
 .
 The pex runtime under .bootstrap/ is not covered by those files: pex
 (Apache-2.0) and the copies it vendors of attrs (MIT), ansicolors (ISC),
 packaging (Apache-2.0 or BSD-2-Clause) and pyparsing (MIT). scripts/build-pex.sh
 fails if that set changes, so this list stays accurate.
 .
 pychrony's compiled extension includes libchrony (LGPL-2.1+). Its source is
 https://gitlab.com/chrony/libchrony, built by pychrony from
 https://github.com/arunderwood/pychrony.

